tasha: Heads-up — I opened a docs PR that switches the dashboard cost breakdown to the new per-trace schema and we need a tiny SDK snippet showing trace->cost correlation for Console observability. PR: https://git.redwood/example/PR-8423. This needs to land before the metrics v2 cutover.

sam: Thanks. Can you paste the exact field names the dashboard expects? I want to make sure the snippet sets the right trace tags.

tasha: The dashboard accepts `trace_id`, `route`, and `cost_usd` in the telemetry event. Ideally snippet shows propagating `trace_id` from incoming request into outbound SDK events and adding a `cost_usd` metric.

miguel: Quick Node example I hacked together — feel free to shorten:```js
// express middleware to attach trace id and cost
app.use((req,res,next)=>{
  const trace = req.headers['x-trace-id'] || generateTraceId();
  telemetry.setTag('trace_id', trace);
  next();
});
// later when recording cost
telemetry.recordMetric('cost_usd', cost, { route: req.path });
telemetry.flush();
```

elaine: Love it. Could we also include a one-liner for Python (requests) showing how to forward `X-Trace-Id` on outbound calls? People copy/paste those a lot. Also note: update the console quickstart 'tracing' note to reference the new `cost_usd` field and add a link to the dashboard JSON.

ben: I can add the Python snippet and land the link fix once CI passes. Will also add a tiny test to docs CI that checks the snippet compiles (lint only).

docs-bot: CI: docs build succeeded — 7 changed files.

tasha: Awesome, thanks everyone. Ben — if you can shepherd this today we can include it in the cutover announcement. :tada:
